{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 53,
  "title": "Hundreds and thousands",
  "description": "Count to a million, and split things in halves and dozens.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Eighty and ninety close the tens, and then come the hundreds and the thousands. A few small words around numbers — half, a dozen, even and odd — finish the system, and after this unit there is no number from zero to a million you cannot say.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eighty and above",
        "body": "Ochenta and noventa work like the other tens. Cien is a hundred on its own, and doscientos and quinientos are two and five hundred. Mil is a thousand and never takes an -s, and un millón is a million.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "ochenta euros",
            "en": "eighty euros"
          },
          {
            "es": "doscientos libros",
            "en": "two hundred books"
          },
          {
            "es": "mil personas",
            "en": "a thousand people"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Around the numbers",
        "body": "Medio is half, and una docena is twelve of something. Par is even and impar is odd. None of them change, and they go where any other number goes.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "medio kilo",
            "en": "half a kilo"
          },
          {
            "es": "una docena de huevos",
            "en": "a dozen eggs"
          },
          {
            "es": "un número par",
            "en": "an even number"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
